# Scratch fixtures `src/providers/native/differential.integration.test.mjs`
# creates directly under this package (not the system tmpdir — see that
# file's header for why), so a run that crashes before its own `afterAll`
# cleanup runs leaves one of these behind instead of vanishing with `/tmp`.
# One stable prefix for every fixture pair's root, present and future
# (`.oracle-<label>-nx-*`, `.oracle-<label>-native-*`, …) — a per-pair prefix
# here would need editing every time a pair is added or renamed, and a stale
# entry left after a rename is a crashed run's leftovers this file no longer
# recognises, which is exactly what `nx show projects` would then see as a
# phantom project in this repository's own tree.
.oracle-*

# `config-spelling.integration.test.mjs`'s A4/A5 ESLint-dialect fixtures need
# the same "under this package, not the system tmpdir" placement, for the same
# `@nx/eslint-plugin` resolution reason — but a different prefix, since they
# do not go through `.oracle-*`'s builders and a crashed run's leftovers would
# otherwise fall through this file unrecognised.
.config-spelling-a4-eslint-*
.config-spelling-a5-eslint-*

# The other two ESLint-dialect fixture roots, each with its own prefix:
# `src/eslint-config.integration.test.mjs`'s `fixtureRoot()` (one per test,
# torn down in `afterEach`) and `src/cli.integration.test.mjs`'s S2 describe
# (one per file, torn down in `afterAll`). Listed here for the reason every
# entry in this file exists: the project walk in
# `src/conformance/boundary.test.mjs` reads its skip list from this file, and
# an unlisted fixture root is one that walk judges as shipped source and races
# the teardown — the intermittent `ENOENT` of #637.
.eslint-config-fixture-*
.cli-eslint-config-fixture-*
